{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"decision\":\"answer\",\"answer\":466,\"evidence\":[\"receipt-1\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"reason\":\"DP counting binary words of length 12 avoiding 000 and 111\"}","reasoning_content":"We need count binary words length 12 that avoid forbidden substrings \"000\" and \"111\". So no three consecutive equal bits. Count sequences of length n with no run of 3 same bits. This is classic recurrence. Let a_n be number of sequences length n ending with run of length 1 of some bit, b_n ending with run length 2. Actually we can do DP: states: last two bits? But easier: Let A_n be sequences length n ending with a single bit (i.e., last two bits different or n=1). Let B_n be sequences ending with two identical bits (run length 2). Then recurrence: For next bit, if we add bit same as last: only allowed if last run length 1. So from A_n we can go to B_{n+1}. If we add different bit: from any state we can go to A_{n+1}. So: A_{n+1} = A_n + B_n (adding different bit). B_{n+1} = A_n (adding same bit). Base: n=1: sequences: \"0\",\"1\". For n=1, run length 1 only. So A_1=2, B_1=0. Compute up to n=12.\n\nLet's iterate.\n\nn=1: A=2 B=0\nn=2: A2 = A1+B1 =2+0=2 ; B2 = A1=2\nn=3: A3 = A2+B2 =2+2=4 ; B3 = A2=2\nn=4: A4 = A3+B3 =4+2=6 ; B4 = A3=4\nn=5: A5 = A4+B4 =6+4=10 ; B5 = A4=6\nn=6: A6 = A5+B5 =10+6=16 ; B6 = A5=10\nn=7: A7 = A6+B6 =16+10=26 ; B7 = A6=16\nn=8: A8 = A7+B7 =26+16=42 ; B8 = A7=26\nn=9: A9 = A8+B8 =42+26=68 ; B9 = A8=42\nn=10: A10 = A9+B9 =68+42=110 ; B10 = A9=68\nn=11: A11 = A10+B10 =110+68=178 ; B11 = A10=110\nn=12: A12 = A11+B11 =178+110=288 ; B12 = A11=178\n\nTotal sequences length 12 = A12 + B12 = 288+178=466.\n\nThus answer 466. Provide final JSON with decision answer."}}],"created":1790985280,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5